 r←GetReadmeSection packagePath;status;sourceUrl;markdown;body;minSize;prefix
⍝ Returns the HTML for the README of the package in `packagePath`, as a vector of character
⍝ vectors, or '' when there is nothing worth showing.
⍝ '' means "leave the section out altogether": no heading, and no notice saying that there
⍝ is no README. A package without one should look like a package that never needed one.
⍝ Too short counts as nothing worth showing. `minSize` is measured against the Markdown
⍝ rather than against the text it renders to, which is an approximation - the Markdown
⍝ carries its own syntax - but a generous one: what it lets through is at worst a little
⍝ shorter than it looks.
 r←''
 minSize←200
 prefix←'readme-'                                   ⍝ Keeps the README's ids clear of the page's own
 (status sourceUrl markdown)←ReadStoredReadme packagePath
 :If 'ok'≢status
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If minSize>≢markdown
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢body←RenderReadme markdown sourceUrl prefix
     :Return
 :EndIf
 r←⊂'<section class="readme">'
 r,←body
⍝ Whoever wrote it gets the credit, and the URL carries the tag, so it also says which
⍝ release this documentation belongs to.
 r,←⊂'<p class="readme-source">README from <a href="',(EscapeAttributeValue sourceUrl),'" rel="nofollow noopener">',(EscapeSpecialChars sourceUrl),'</a></p>'
 r,←⊂'</section>'
